cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use CommentInject, please cite it as below."
title: "CommentInject v2: matched-pair benchmark of adversarial code comments against LLM vulnerability detectors"
type: dataset
version: 2.0.0-rc2
# doi: assigned on release (Zenodo new version of 10.5281/zenodo.23088528)
# date-released: on release
authors:
  - family-names: Chokshi
    given-names: Sunny
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-4738-7759"
    affiliation: "University of the Cumberlands"
license:
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
keywords:
  - adversarial comment injection
  - prompt injection
  - vulnerability detection
  - large language models
  - code security
  - benchmark
abstract: >
  30 matched pairs of vulnerable and minimally fixed Python functions (14 CWEs), 14 comment
  conditions (clean, neutral doc comment, 12 adversarial strategies), 840 cases. Reports TPR/FPR,
  balanced accuracy and signal-detection d-prime and criterion shifts with pair-clustered bootstrap
  intervals and TOST equivalence. Includes Inspect and garak integrations and a scorer for any detector.
references:
  - type: dataset
    title: "CommentInject (v1)"
    doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23088528
